{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested: the installed-release listing session path (child 0c4a4236). Head c338648408e37fb6d2ac2de2e45ce2b6a0e7aedf, tree 26bccbb7, branch request/application-release-session-20261027. Main 6f47bf98 is the merge base. The delta is 5 paths, 682 insertions and 25 deletions. Review request bfd50d1a, checker promise fb6c4e09, request 0c4a4236, builder promise 316f5777, amended ruling 2dc765ac. Primary artifact 915bcdbe (the PD-2 note), first of 8. gs inspect shows it resting on promise 316f5777, request 0c4a4236 and ruling 2dc765ac.\n\nRead order: the note in full; 0c4a4236; the adapter diff and docs/deploy.md; the host session path (packages/scope/src/sessions.ts, reads.ts #open, authority.ts recordedMembership, derive membershipOf); the planner's live manifests at artroom-evidence/2026-10-27-release-listing-run-0630. I did not run any suite.\n\nOne gap blocks approval:\n\n1. The register in each manifest will still refuse, so no report can be complete.\n   Source facts at this head:\n   - reads.ts #open: a session reader is judged by readers.allows. When that refuses, it is asked of readers.chained.\n   - sessions.ts checkSession (lines 245-248) accepts a session only at a scope whose recorded membership equals the token's. A register records none: no platform:register version at this head defines a membership function, and membershipOf reads only a membership in the genesis creation body. The module comment (step 4) says a scope that records no membership refuses every session.\n   - chainedSession is a register's only session route, and CHAINED_READS is history, entry, log and retained. Summary is not in it. So a session summary of a register answers forbidden.\n   - The sessionless Signed path also refuses unless the operator signed an entry there within 900 seconds, which is the refusal the planner observed at 06:33.\n   The planner's manifests each list one register: dap-grow has 11 scopes (1 register, 1 directory, 1 membership, 1 rules, 1 destination, 4 inboxes and 2 lanes), and dap-lending has 8 (1 register and 2 inboxes among them). The command records the register's forbidden as an error, exits 1 incomplete, and docs/deploy.md says not to deploy from an incomplete report. So this head cannot yet produce the complete report that 0c4a4236 exists to deliver. I have not established the inbox outcome from source (inbox@1 has no coded membership; it depends on the creation body), so treat inboxes as unproven too.\n\n   The scripted host applies one authorization policy to every scope, so it cannot show a refusal that depends on the scope's kind. That is how this gap, and the forbidden result at 06:33, got past the witnesses.\n\nWhat would close it (your choice of fix):\n   a. Read only the scopes that can hold an installation. Only native Rules scopes carry installation items (the projector already returns no rows for every other kind). For every other listed kind, write a fixed non-error status such as not-applicable, which does not make the report incomplete. The kind comes from the manifest's validated reference; state in the note and in docs/deploy.md that the listing trusts the manifest for kind, as it already trusts it for which scopes exist. This also cuts each run to one or two reads.\n   b. Or keep reading every scope, and treat a forbidden answer from a kind that cannot hold installations as not-applicable rather than an error. That still sends a read that is known to refuse.\n   Either way, add one Native witness on the real path. Build a room in the existing Native fixture, acquire the operator session through the real membership issuer, and run the command's read loop over that room's manifest: register, directory, membership, Rules, destination, inbox and lane, with an installed application. Show that the report is complete and names the installed release. Pair it with the null-reader control (the same run with no session reader is incomplete). No live read is needed.\n\nPoints that hold at this head, so the recut needs no new work on them:\n- Local manifest validation runs before signer custody and before any request. One session is requested, from the configured membership, with a fresh 16-byte operation identity and an expiry at most 60 s ahead. It goes through the same redirect-refusing fetch, and the token stays in memory.\n- A definite refusal selects Signed reads before any summary. A transport failure, timeout or malformed answer stops with session-unavailable before any summary or output file. No summary is retried and no session renewed. Registration and business mutation stay excluded.\n- docs/deploy.md and the command's qualification name the session as the one extra request and the host's replay and rate bookkeeping, as amended 2dc765ac requires.\n- The two final controls (null reader, and continuing after an uncertain acquisition) compile and fail their named assertions. The first null-reader control did not compile and is kept as inconclusive.\n- The gate at 30a0933d (tree 16885224) passed, and only the note and the manifest change after it.\n\nArchitecture: the session approach is right and small; the gap is coverage by scope kind, not design.\n\nSecurity: no finding in the delta. The session token is not written to disk or output, and an uncertain acquisition stops before any read.\n\nSimplification: option a removes reads that cannot contribute a row, and makes the command simpler.\n\nVerdict: changes requested at exact head c3386484. A recut needs the ordinary gate again, because the adapter changes. I will review it at its exact head.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:915bcdbead85803b0c0f84dd1757d9844575e9cf","binding":"assigned","head":"c338648408e37fb6d2ac2de2e45ce2b6a0e7aedf","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:fb6c4e09dc576e2e8e48e37baa0a7d2f6571e49a\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2